1
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:03,960
NATSUKIYA
RAMEN

2
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:04,880
Why?

3
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:07,130
Why not go with your usual
clear-broth shoyu ramen!

4
00:00:07,590 --> 00:00:10,720
Why do you want the rich seafood
and tonkotsu thick broth tsukemen?

5
00:00:11,090 --> 00:00:14,470
A soldier's thirst
can't be quenched with this!

6
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:16,220
Ya idiot!

7
00:00:16,220 --> 00:00:19,100
Tsukemen has always been
the thing for the front line!

8
00:00:30,530 --> 00:00:31,860
Why...

9
00:00:31,860 --> 00:00:33,450
Seafood and tonkotsu...

10
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:34,990
Their throats...

11
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:10,000
THE IMPOSSIBLE AFTERMATH
OF AN IMPOSSIBLE GAME / SATURDAY, JUNE 6th

12
00:02:13,340 --> 00:02:15,090
I'm begging you, Noren!

13
00:02:15,090 --> 00:02:16,630
Don't wake up quite yet!

14
00:02:17,090 --> 00:02:20,850
Noren Mitsuoka is already hypnotized.

15
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:26,390
When she wakes, she will fall in love
with the first person she sees!

16
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:28,230
The hell?

17
00:02:28,230 --> 00:02:31,940
Eiji Rindou's a given,
but don't look at Tenma, either!

18
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:32,770
If you look...

19
00:02:32,770 --> 00:02:33,610
MINCEMEAT / LOVE / LOVE / LOVE
PRETENDING TO DATE

20
00:02:33,610 --> 00:02:36,110
...the relationship chart
will get way too confusing!

21
00:02:36,110 --> 00:02:38,860
Things will get awkward
in the home ec club!

22
00:02:45,830 --> 00:02:47,120
CHASHU TOPPING

23
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:48,040
Huh?

24
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:50,500
Why are you filling the barrels
with chashu pork?

25
00:02:50,830 --> 00:02:52,380
This is for peace!

26
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:54,050
I can't fire that anymore!

27
00:02:54,050 --> 00:02:55,340
Are you sure?

28
00:02:55,340 --> 00:02:58,510
I think you can fire if you tried!
Are you sure?

29
00:02:58,930 --> 00:02:59,760
Hm?

30
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:05,520
Powdered fish?

31
00:03:06,020 --> 00:03:06,930
Huh?

32
00:03:09,890 --> 00:03:10,850
Oh...

33
00:03:10,850 --> 00:03:11,940
You're right.

34
00:03:15,480 --> 00:03:17,360
Stop it!

35
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:22,070
Powdered fish...
makes customers thirsty.

36
00:03:42,550 --> 00:03:43,800
Time out!

37
00:03:44,390 --> 00:03:45,810
Let's catch our breaths!

38
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:49,730
Sorry for tossing this to you!

39
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:55,480
I bought these before coming here.

40
00:03:56,820 --> 00:03:59,900
Anyway, this guy's incredible!

41
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:03,490
I've never golfed before,
but he seems really good at it!

42
00:04:04,070 --> 00:04:09,200
That kind of accuracy and power
isn't something you can learn in a day.

43
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:11,120
He should try becoming a pro golfer!

44
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:14,500
I don't really know this guy's deal...

45
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:21,010
but he's the type who can choose
whether or not he kills someone.

46
00:04:21,010 --> 00:04:24,390
It sucks, considering
he's got all that skill...

47
00:04:24,390 --> 00:04:27,760
and I don't want to fight him
when I'm feeling like this.

48
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:33,520
MY NOTE BOOK
CRAYONS

49
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:36,860
AGREED

50
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:38,190
"Agreed"...

51
00:04:38,190 --> 00:04:40,110
Wait, you can give a piece of your mind!

52
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,240
YOU'RE AMAZING. DON'T WANNA KILL YOU.

53
00:04:41,240 --> 00:04:44,610
"You're amazing. Don't wanna kill you."

54
00:04:44,610 --> 00:04:45,240
Wha...

55
00:04:45,530 --> 00:04:47,490
Then let's stop all this crap!

56
00:04:47,490 --> 00:04:48,580
BUT I CAN'T DITCH MY MISSION.

57
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:52,500
"But I can't ditch my mission."

58
00:04:52,790 --> 00:04:57,090
"And can't think hard now."

59
00:04:57,090 --> 00:04:57,880
AND CAN'T THINK HARD NOW.
MY BROTHER IS TRYING TO FIX THAT.

60
00:04:57,880 --> 00:05:00,510
"My brother is trying to fix that."

61
00:05:00,510 --> 00:05:01,130
I WANNA FIX, TOO.

62
00:05:01,130 --> 00:05:03,130
"I wanna fix, too."

63
00:05:03,130 --> 00:05:06,640
"Want it to end for him."

64
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:08,640
"He's a bit scary..."

65
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:09,260
"HE'S A BIT SCARY, BUT MY BROTHER
IS THE MOST IMPORTANT TO ME."

66
00:05:09,260 --> 00:05:13,140
"...but my brother
is the most important to me."

67
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:18,860
You got me there!

68
00:05:19,230 --> 00:05:21,030
I can't pull back!

69
00:05:21,030 --> 00:05:23,900
And I'm not a good negotiator!

70
00:05:24,650 --> 00:05:28,830
I really shouldn't learn about 
the opponent before my match.

71
00:05:29,490 --> 00:05:31,160
That doesn't mean...

72
00:05:31,580 --> 00:05:34,080
it's okay for me to lose, though!

73
00:05:34,790 --> 00:05:35,620
Well...

74
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:37,630
Let's get back to the game!

75
00:05:39,250 --> 00:05:40,170
Tenma!

76
00:05:40,170 --> 00:05:41,000
Are you okay?

77
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:43,300
Ogami! What about you?

78
00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:45,130
Yeah! I'm done on my end!

79
00:05:45,130 --> 00:05:45,760
Huh?

80
00:05:46,380 --> 00:05:47,680
What about Noren?

81
00:05:48,050 --> 00:05:48,760
Huh?

82
00:05:50,050 --> 00:05:52,390
Good! She's not awake yet!

83
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:55,520
You're done? That means...

84
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:56,440
Yeah!

85
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:58,270
I took out the older brother.

86
00:05:59,940 --> 00:06:02,650
Boss, that's the worst way to put it!

87
00:06:02,650 --> 00:06:03,940
You haven't killed him!

88
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:06,570
Oh, sorry. Old habits.

89
00:06:32,970 --> 00:06:36,640
Ogami! Don't tell me you...
fought the other one and killed—

90
00:06:36,640 --> 00:06:37,730
Did not!

91
00:06:37,730 --> 00:06:39,650
I just knocked his lights out!

92
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:44,360
But I think that guy thinks
you killed his big bro!

93
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:48,910
He snapped and started shooting everywhere!

94
00:06:49,570 --> 00:06:53,660
That makes the balls harder to dodge
and impossible to shoot down!

95
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:56,200
Shit, how am I gonna stop this?

96
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:57,540
A few shots into his limbs?

97
00:06:57,870 --> 00:06:59,710
No, a headshot?

98
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:02,960
In either case,
I can't let Tenma see blood!

99
00:07:03,340 --> 00:07:05,420
Ogami! Let me take over!

100
00:07:05,420 --> 00:07:06,170
Huh?

101
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:07,880
Get his attention...

102
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:09,300
even for just a few seconds!

103
00:07:09,930 --> 00:07:12,800
And I'll show you a real killer shot!

104
00:07:16,970 --> 00:07:18,100
Hey, over here!

105
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:19,440
Drive that ball at me!

106
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:27,780
Boss?

107
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,610
No problem!

108
00:07:35,950 --> 00:07:38,750
A killer shot? For real?

109
00:07:39,290 --> 00:07:42,040
But Tenma ain't the type to call bluffs.

110
00:07:42,460 --> 00:07:44,210
If you're saying you can do it...

111
00:07:44,210 --> 00:07:45,420
I believe you.

112
00:07:46,250 --> 00:07:48,970
Soccer's another type of game
where you can put spin on the ball.

113
00:07:48,970 --> 00:07:52,300
For example, there are banana kicks
and knuckleball shots.

114
00:07:53,300 --> 00:07:57,180
But there is one type of spin
you almost never see in soccer.

115
00:07:57,720 --> 00:07:58,890
You know what that is?

116
00:07:59,230 --> 00:08:01,810
No clue. Never thought about it.

117
00:08:03,310 --> 00:08:04,440
A spiral!

118
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:06,190
In other words, a gyro spin!

119
00:08:06,730 --> 00:08:08,280
It's just like a bullet.

120
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:11,780
Making the ball spiral around
 the direction it's traveling

121
00:08:12,410 --> 00:08:15,490
really ups it penetration potential.

122
00:08:15,870 --> 00:08:17,370
At least on paper.

123
00:08:18,330 --> 00:08:21,410
You just came up with that
while fooling around, right?

124
00:08:21,410 --> 00:08:23,580
Quit acting like you're smart.

125
00:08:36,430 --> 00:08:37,220
For real?

126
00:08:47,060 --> 00:08:49,480
You cracked concrete!

127
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:50,610
How's that?

128
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:53,070
It's powerful, but it leaves me wide open.

129
00:08:53,070 --> 00:08:56,200
So, I can't use it during a game.

130
00:08:56,570 --> 00:08:57,910
That's useless.

131
00:09:01,790 --> 00:09:04,870
Sorry man, but I'm putting an end to this!

132
00:09:08,710 --> 00:09:14,590
Super Gyro Spin Shot!

133
00:09:57,260 --> 00:09:58,680
Damn, seriously?

134
00:09:59,430 --> 00:10:03,680
He just took out a JARDIN hitman!

135
00:10:06,520 --> 00:10:08,310
We somehow got through it,

136
00:10:08,310 --> 00:10:10,650
but this mess...

137
00:10:10,650 --> 00:10:12,570
What the hell are we gonna do?

138
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:13,780
Ogami!

139
00:10:14,110 --> 00:10:16,570
I have so much I wanna ask you!

140
00:10:16,570 --> 00:10:19,950
You know what's up
with these guys, don't you?

141
00:10:19,950 --> 00:10:21,490
Well, um...

142
00:10:21,490 --> 00:10:22,330
Boss...

143
00:10:22,330 --> 00:10:24,620
We can't clean up this mess!
We're totally screwed!

144
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:25,790
- Huh?
- Huh?

145
00:10:27,500 --> 00:10:29,000
Morning.

146
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,290
Huh?

147
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:33,130
Ogami?

148
00:10:51,060 --> 00:10:51,690
Oh...

149
00:10:52,020 --> 00:10:53,900
U-Um...

150
00:10:53,900 --> 00:10:55,150
What the...

151
00:10:55,150 --> 00:10:57,820
Why was I asleep here of all places?

152
00:10:58,280 --> 00:10:59,320
That's right!

153
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:02,660
I was suddenly assaulted
by two guys in the movie theater.

154
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:10,540
Don't tell me...

155
00:11:10,540 --> 00:11:12,790
You saved me again.

156
00:11:13,130 --> 00:11:14,250
Nope.

157
00:11:14,250 --> 00:11:15,340
It wasn't me.

158
00:11:15,340 --> 00:11:17,510
I'm so happy! Thank you!

159
00:11:17,840 --> 00:11:19,930
I helped, too.

160
00:11:20,590 --> 00:11:21,890
"Again"?

161
00:11:21,890 --> 00:11:26,640
Damn, this girl might be catching on
that he saved her in the past!

162
00:11:26,970 --> 00:11:29,690
This keeps getting worse
on so many levels!

163
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:32,690
Oh, I'm sorry!
I was so happy I couldn't help it!

164
00:11:33,110 --> 00:11:34,070
Nope.

165
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:37,570
Boss, have you been trembling
for the past few minutes?

166
00:11:37,570 --> 00:11:39,950
O-Of course I am!

167
00:11:39,950 --> 00:11:42,870
I told you Noren is the same age
as my daughter!

168
00:11:42,870 --> 00:11:45,660
That's enough of a reason
to not be okay with this!

169
00:11:45,660 --> 00:11:47,580
I mean, if it was a five-year-old...

170
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:49,790
Papa, I love you!

171
00:11:49,790 --> 00:11:51,370
I wanna marry you!

172
00:11:51,670 --> 00:11:54,210
I'm so happy! I love you, too!

173
00:11:54,710 --> 00:11:57,340
...now that'd be okay!
That's totally heartwarming!

174
00:11:57,340 --> 00:12:00,220
I'm sure that's a good daddy
who really loves his kid! Good for him!

175
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:03,840
But when they get to a sensible age,

176
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:06,640
and say the same thing
in a serious voice...

177
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:10,060
I really do want to marry you, Papa!

178
00:12:10,060 --> 00:12:11,230
You're kidding me?

179
00:12:11,230 --> 00:12:12,390
I'm serious!

180
00:12:12,390 --> 00:12:13,480
Why?

181
00:12:13,850 --> 00:12:16,980
Now that would send shivers
down any normal dad's spine!

182
00:12:16,980 --> 00:12:20,030
Any guy who's into that goes
to a special place in Hell after he dies!

183
00:12:20,030 --> 00:12:21,110
Well, probably!

184
00:12:21,530 --> 00:12:22,950
B-B-Boss...

185
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:25,200
A hitman is talking about Hell?

186
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:27,160
In either case, we...

187
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:30,330
I don't need a grim remark like that!
I know all too well!

188
00:12:31,210 --> 00:12:32,460
Ogami...

189
00:12:33,670 --> 00:12:36,500
Maybe this is like
the suspension bridge effect.

190
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:37,920
I don't get it...

191
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:40,840
but my heart's been racing
for a while now!

192
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:43,090
This might not be
something I should say now...

193
00:12:43,090 --> 00:12:44,090
but maybe...

194
00:12:44,090 --> 00:12:45,680
Just maybe...

195
00:12:45,680 --> 00:12:47,470
Ogami, I might be...

196
00:12:47,470 --> 00:12:48,970
f-falling in—

197
00:12:49,270 --> 00:12:50,220
- Huh?
- Huh?

198
00:12:53,140 --> 00:12:54,310
What?

199
00:12:54,310 --> 00:12:56,230
What the hell are you doing, Ogami?

200
00:12:56,610 --> 00:13:00,150
Even from my perspective,
you guys had something going!

201
00:13:00,150 --> 00:13:01,740
What's with the karate chop to the neck?

202
00:13:01,740 --> 00:13:03,240
Oh, there was a mosquito.

203
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:04,700
You slap mosquitos!

204
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:06,740
You don't karate chop them!

205
00:13:07,070 --> 00:13:10,120
Is it really okay to save the heroine
and then knock her out?

206
00:13:11,870 --> 00:13:14,750
I was so confident in my
brother's victory heading over.

207
00:13:15,370 --> 00:13:18,540
I never thought it would end up this way.

208
00:13:18,540 --> 00:13:20,750
Kazuma Rindou! What the hell...

209
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:22,210
Hold on a sec, Ogami!

210
00:13:22,210 --> 00:13:22,920
Huh?

211
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:24,760
Something's weird about him!

212
00:13:25,300 --> 00:13:28,010
Why's he wearing Chisato's clothes?

213
00:13:28,010 --> 00:13:30,680
Oh, no. These aren't hers.

214
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:32,100
I bought the same outfit.

215
00:13:32,100 --> 00:13:33,310
Wait, hold up!

216
00:13:33,310 --> 00:13:35,140
We'll talk about that later.

217
00:13:35,140 --> 00:13:37,020
Calm down, Tenma.

218
00:13:39,690 --> 00:13:41,530
Well, indeed.

219
00:13:41,530 --> 00:13:44,700
Now that it's come to this,
there's only one thing to do.

220
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:46,160
Plead for my life.

221
00:13:46,570 --> 00:13:47,870
- Huh?
- Huh?

222
00:13:49,990 --> 00:13:53,870
I beg of you. I'll be fine.
I'll do anything.

223
00:13:53,870 --> 00:13:56,540
So, please, Eiji's life if nothing else.

224
00:13:56,540 --> 00:13:58,920
Can you spare him?

225
00:13:59,420 --> 00:14:03,880
In our world,
failure or defeat means death.

226
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:07,130
I've resolved to accept my fate,

227
00:14:07,130 --> 00:14:08,550
but even so...

228
00:14:08,550 --> 00:14:11,560
I wanna fight
for my brother's life to the end!

229
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:14,060
Please!

230
00:14:14,430 --> 00:14:18,770
Well, um... I didn't intend
to do that to begin with.

231
00:14:18,770 --> 00:14:20,690
Huh? Are you asking Ogami?

232
00:14:20,690 --> 00:14:22,190
I didn't, either!

233
00:14:22,190 --> 00:14:25,900
I'm not thinking of taking time
to deliver a killing blow after all this!

234
00:14:31,910 --> 00:14:33,330
And there ya have it.

235
00:14:33,950 --> 00:14:37,290
We gotta talk, so I can't tell you
to go home just yet.

236
00:14:37,290 --> 00:14:40,130
But when it's over, you can
take him away wherever you want.

237
00:14:42,960 --> 00:14:44,510
I see.

238
00:14:44,510 --> 00:14:46,590
Apologies.

239
00:14:47,590 --> 00:14:49,300
You have my gratitude.

240
00:14:51,970 --> 00:14:55,310
Now, I said "when it's over."

241
00:14:55,310 --> 00:14:57,600
It's far from over. 
This place is a huge mess.

242
00:14:58,230 --> 00:14:59,900
I think I'm about to cry.

243
00:15:00,270 --> 00:15:02,360
What do we do now?

244
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:04,070
Wait. Hold on just a minute!

245
00:15:04,360 --> 00:15:07,360
Before we do anything,
there's something I gotta ask.

246
00:15:07,360 --> 00:15:09,240
Who the hell are you guys?

247
00:15:09,740 --> 00:15:12,700
I was thinking while we were fighting
that you guys aren't normal.

248
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:17,830
At first, you seemed like
 bad guys out to kidnap Noren.

249
00:15:17,830 --> 00:15:21,210
But you guys are on a different level
from thugs or the yakuza.

250
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:24,960
Ogami, you seem to know a bit
of what's going on, too.

251
00:15:25,300 --> 00:15:26,340
Just maybe...

252
00:15:26,710 --> 00:15:29,340
You're from the same world as these guys?

253
00:15:30,590 --> 00:15:31,590
Boss!

254
00:15:31,590 --> 00:15:33,050
Maybe Kazuma might...

255
00:15:33,050 --> 00:15:33,970
Right!

256
00:15:34,310 --> 00:15:39,100
Hey, can you make him forget everything
about today with your hypnosis?

257
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:41,600
Huh? I can do that, but...

258
00:15:41,900 --> 00:15:43,980
Please, just do it!

259
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:52,450
I will count to three.

260
00:15:52,450 --> 00:15:55,120
When I finish counting and 
you hear the lighter close,

261
00:15:55,660 --> 00:15:57,660
you will instantly fall asleep.

262
00:15:57,660 --> 00:16:00,250
When you wake up, you'll have
 forgetten everything about today.

263
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:02,210
Three...

264
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:03,670
two...

265
00:16:04,170 --> 00:16:05,250
one.

266
00:16:15,390 --> 00:16:18,100
What the hell was that
just now? Cut it out!

267
00:16:18,100 --> 00:16:19,980
Huh? It's not working?

268
00:16:19,980 --> 00:16:20,730
What?

269
00:16:20,730 --> 00:16:22,520
O-One more time!

270
00:16:23,230 --> 00:16:24,020
Hey.

271
00:16:24,020 --> 00:16:25,190
Once more!

272
00:16:26,070 --> 00:16:27,980
I told you!

273
00:16:29,940 --> 00:16:30,990
This guy...

274
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:32,700
Impossible!

275
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:35,120
My hypnosis... isn't working!

276
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:36,030
Huh?

277
00:16:36,030 --> 00:16:37,450
What's going on here?

278
00:16:37,450 --> 00:16:40,950
You were saying
you were good, cheap, and fast!

279
00:16:40,950 --> 00:16:43,120
I never said I was like a beef bowl chain!

280
00:16:43,540 --> 00:16:46,340
I said "anyone...
powerfully and instantly"!

281
00:16:46,710 --> 00:16:48,800
But this is a first for me!

282
00:16:48,800 --> 00:16:50,880
What is up with this guy?

283
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:52,630
He is way too extraordinary!

284
00:16:52,930 --> 00:16:54,220
B-Boss...

285
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:55,800
At this point...

286
00:16:55,800 --> 00:16:57,470
I just gotta laugh.

287
00:16:57,810 --> 00:16:59,600
That's the way Tenma is.

288
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:05,400
I gotta say the jig is up for real now.

289
00:17:07,270 --> 00:17:09,400
Hitmen?

290
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:12,150
Guys like that really exist?

291
00:17:12,690 --> 00:17:16,160
<i>B-Boss, was it really okay to tell him?</i>

292
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:17,950
It ain't good.

293
00:17:17,950 --> 00:17:19,950
I can't go to school anymore.

294
00:17:19,950 --> 00:17:23,500
The mission is over,
and I'm unemployed starting tomorrow.

295
00:17:24,370 --> 00:17:26,420
It's all over as of today.

296
00:17:26,750 --> 00:17:29,880
Sorry for trying to hypnotize you earlier.

297
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:33,340
And you have my thanks
for helping me save Noren.

298
00:17:35,010 --> 00:17:37,510
Ogami, you're going to go away, too?

299
00:17:41,010 --> 00:17:42,020
Yeah.

300
00:17:43,020 --> 00:17:43,890
Huh?

301
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:47,400
It's bad for a hitman to come to school?

302
00:17:47,690 --> 00:17:48,730
- Huh?
- Huh?

303
00:17:48,730 --> 00:17:51,780
I mean, killing people
is something you should never do.

304
00:17:51,780 --> 00:17:53,650
More like, stop doing that right now.

305
00:17:53,650 --> 00:17:56,490
But isn't that all the more reason
for you to go to school?

306
00:17:56,490 --> 00:17:58,280
So you can find a different career path?

307
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:01,660
You were going because 
you had to for work, right?

308
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:04,080
At least, that's
what it looked like to me.

309
00:18:05,330 --> 00:18:08,710
I know that you quitting now won't make
everything you did in the past okay.

310
00:18:08,710 --> 00:18:09,330
BUT I CAN'T DITCH MY MISSION.

311
00:18:09,330 --> 00:18:10,790
AND CAN'T THINK HARD NOW.
MY BROTHER IS TRYING TO FIX THAT.

312
00:18:10,790 --> 00:18:11,880
But in the end...

313
00:18:11,880 --> 00:18:15,220
I don't think you guys are all that bad.

314
00:18:16,180 --> 00:18:19,430
I mean, you like school
and studying, right?

315
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:22,260
Then don't give up on that.

316
00:18:22,260 --> 00:18:26,060
You can change, look ahead,
and come to school again.

317
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:28,310
I won't blow your cover or anything.

318
00:18:29,810 --> 00:18:31,440
What's with them?

319
00:18:31,770 --> 00:18:33,610
First Master, then Big Sis...

320
00:18:33,610 --> 00:18:35,240
and this guy, too?

321
00:18:35,570 --> 00:18:39,070
I can't tell who's the adult
and who's the kid.

322
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:41,200
No.

323
00:18:41,530 --> 00:18:45,790
Maybe stuff like that
 doesn't matter at all.

324
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:51,750
I've been taught so much
ever since I started going to school.

325
00:18:53,250 --> 00:18:55,550
And that goes for you brothers, too!

326
00:18:55,550 --> 00:18:57,840
You can't kill! Ever!

327
00:18:57,840 --> 00:18:59,930
Oh, you're right.

328
00:19:01,510 --> 00:19:05,180
What you're saying... is something
my brother might also say.

329
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:06,850
- Huh?
- Oh!

330
00:19:07,180 --> 00:19:08,270
Sirens?

331
00:19:08,270 --> 00:19:09,230
Hey, Kazuma!

332
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:13,110
No, this isn't one of my tricks.

333
00:19:13,110 --> 00:19:14,980
It's a real report.

334
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:16,990
You guys go out the back.

335
00:19:16,990 --> 00:19:17,610
Huh?

336
00:19:18,110 --> 00:19:20,490
I have hypnosis.

337
00:19:20,820 --> 00:19:24,240
Coming up with a story
to cover my ass is easy for me.

338
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:27,750
I was already planning 
on doing that anyway.

339
00:19:27,750 --> 00:19:29,080
But...

340
00:19:29,080 --> 00:19:30,370
You might fail.

341
00:19:30,370 --> 00:19:32,380
Tenma is an exception!

342
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:37,970
No, we're not done quite yet!

343
00:19:37,970 --> 00:19:40,550
Undo the hypnosis you put on Noren!

344
00:19:40,550 --> 00:19:42,550
Sorry, got no time for that!

345
00:19:42,550 --> 00:19:44,220
I'll take care of that next time!

346
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:44,890
Huh?

347
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:48,100
I've already put in
the paperwork...

348
00:19:48,100 --> 00:19:50,140
so I'll be seeing you again soon enough.

349
00:19:50,600 --> 00:19:54,770
There's no doubt that the girl
is a clue for me to cure my brother.

350
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:57,150
I'll forego the duel for now...

351
00:19:57,150 --> 00:19:59,490
but in the near future...

352
00:19:59,490 --> 00:20:01,280
we'll be transferring to your school.

353
00:20:01,700 --> 00:20:03,820
Really? I'm counting on that!

354
00:20:03,820 --> 00:20:06,410
It better be sooner
than just the near future, too!

355
00:20:15,540 --> 00:20:17,460
Are you all right?

356
00:20:17,460 --> 00:20:18,460
Are you hurt?

357
00:20:19,550 --> 00:20:21,050
Are you okay, too?

358
00:20:21,630 --> 00:20:22,930
Are you hurt—

359
00:22:35,890 --> 00:22:37,100
MODERN MIDDLE SCHOOL
MATH 1

360
00:22:37,100 --> 00:22:40,810
Man, that was one hellish weekend!

361
00:22:40,810 --> 00:22:42,610
Tell me about it.

362
00:22:42,610 --> 00:22:46,320
It's great that you can go back
to school again!

363
00:22:46,320 --> 00:22:47,900
One way or another.

364
00:22:48,530 --> 00:22:53,330
In the end, even putting my age aside,
Tenma caught on to my job.

365
00:22:53,330 --> 00:22:57,290
And it's entirely likely that hitmen
targeting Noren will drop by again.

366
00:22:57,960 --> 00:23:02,170
We really need to rethink
a lot of stuff here.

367
00:23:02,840 --> 00:23:04,130
Besides...

368
00:23:04,130 --> 00:23:06,470
This case ain't over yet.

369
00:23:06,470 --> 00:23:11,430
Sounds like the Rindou brothers will be
transferring to this middle school, too.

370
00:23:12,350 --> 00:23:13,810
Ogami...

371
00:23:14,640 --> 00:23:18,310
But until then,
Noren is still under hypnosis.

372
00:23:18,310 --> 00:23:21,650
On top of it, the spell puts her
into 100% serious love mode,

373
00:23:21,650 --> 00:23:23,150
so she's strangely assertive!

374
00:23:24,690 --> 00:23:28,610
Starting today, I can't drop my guard
at school even for an instant.

375
00:23:28,610 --> 00:23:30,200
Why don't you just stay home?

376
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:32,120
No way. I wanna study.

377
00:23:33,370 --> 00:23:36,450
Whatever happens,
I have to do everything in my power...

378
00:23:36,450 --> 00:23:39,040
to avoid even accidentally advancing
my relationship with Noren!

